{
  "requirement": "The `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents, once every group is decided, to commit the agreed requirements of all groups in one commit before any implementation, leaving out uncommitted edits the user said do not belong to the task.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has four obligations for the `habeas-requirements` skill. The reviewed test `the_requirements_skill_commits_every_group_together_before_code` in `tests/authoring_cli.rs` covers each one.\n\n- **One commit for all groups, before any code.** `step_of` panics unless a workflow step contains \"then commit it, all groups together, before any code\". In `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md`, step 5 (\"Commit\") contains that phrase, so the test fails if the wording is removed or changed.\n- **Only once every group is decided.** The test asserts that the commit step comes after the step containing `**Gate:**`. In the skill, the gate is in step 4 and says there is no commit until the user has agreed to, rejected or deferred every group. A skill that allowed an earlier commit would fail this ordering check.\n- **Leave out unrelated edits.** The test asserts that the commit step contains \"leave out unrelated edits found in step 1\". Step 1 is where the skill asks the user whether uncommitted edits belong to the task, so this ties the exclusion to the user's answer. Removing or moving the exclusion would fail the test.\n- **Ordering against implementation.** The test does not assert that the commit comes before \"Implement and test\", but the phrase \"before any code\" is checked. A sibling test, `the_requirements_skill_commits_agreed_requirements_before_code`, also asserts `gate < commit < implement`. It is marked for the parent requirement, so it is only supporting evidence.\n\nThe test is a phrase-and-ordering check on the skill text. That is the only way to check a directive written in prose. I found no plausible change to the skill's wording that violates the requirement and still passes these assertions, so I found no gap.",
  "references": "8607d5bca7a6f77d7c1cc7bd0259728f9914c910f5ef7ee60fb0af8a17800a7a",
